{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-164350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(-1,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }x\\ge 0}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(-1,4)$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(1,-4)$"] ["text" "A parabola centered at $(1,-4)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbola centered at $(-1,4)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $5$ and $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "An ellipse centered at $(0,-3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $25$ and $9.$"] ["text" "An ellipse centered at $(0,-3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $5$ and $3.$"] ["text" "An ellipse centered at $(0,3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $5$ and $3.$"] ["text" "The interior and boundary of an ellipse centered at $(0,-3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $25$ and $9.$"] ["text" "The interior and boundary of an ellipse centered at $(0,3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $5$ and $3.$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An ellipse centered at $(0,3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $5$ and $3.$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "An ellipse centered at $(-1,2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["text" "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $4.$"] ["text" "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["text" "The interior and boundary of an ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["text" "The interior and boundary of an ellipse centered at $(1,2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2.$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(-5,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:xy=1}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(-5,0)$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(5,0)$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(5,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbola centered at $(-5,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x-1)^{2}=3y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}=3y,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(x-1)^{2}=3y}.\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164419" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164419" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}^{2}"] ["text" "A rightward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(-1,0)$"] ["text" "A rightward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0)$"] ["text" "An upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(-1,0)$"] ["text" "An upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164419" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2}=10$ and the plane $z=5$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=5,$ we substitute $z=5$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$10$ and $5$"] ["text" "$5$ and $2$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{2}$ and $1$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic cylinder $9{x}^{2}+2(y-1)^{2}=18$ and the plane $z=1$ onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=1,$ we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+2(y-1)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(3)^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{2}$ and $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-35363" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35363" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$2$ and $6$"] ["text" "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $6$"] ["text" "$4$ and $3$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$"] ["text" "$\\sqrt{2}$ and $4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-35363" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =3\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =1,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $x=1$ and $x=5$ in the $xy$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1$"] ["text" "The hyperbola $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1$"] ["text" "The line $x=3$"] ["text" "The line $x=5$"] ["text" "The lines $x=1$ and $x=5$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The lines $x=1$ and $x=5$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x+3)^{2}=6y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =6y \\\\ 9 & =6y \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{6} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a line in the $yz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The line $y=3$"] ["text" "The line $y=\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "The lines $y=-3$ and $y=15$"] ["text" "The parabola $(x+3)^{2}=6z$"] ["text" "The parabola ${x}^{2}=6(z-3)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The line $y=\\frac{3}{2}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2}=12$ and the plane $y=1$ onto the $xz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $y=1,$ we substitute $y=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $y$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4782647455488501747973bb60105f1dcaa7f75feb8168490f00f706ebd51482"} {"question" "q-164411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$2$ and $1$"] ["text" "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "$4$ and $1$"] ["text" "$4$ and $2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "q-164411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c701b98c5fc0cafefefcd8e6d7c2f1838da1464b98b45a77e373181936431b6"} {"question" "e-8226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/example-8226.json" "file_sha256" "38fdb783a049c5d4a3a1b656009ea7be9c43bf3fa9eef18ab402398f2144f537"} {"question" "e-8226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1, \\qquad z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\dfrac{x^2}{3^2} + \\dfrac{(y+1)^2}{1^2} = 1\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,-1)$ with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/example-8226.json" "file_sha256" "38fdb783a049c5d4a3a1b656009ea7be9c43bf3fa9eef18ab402398f2144f537"} {"question" "e-8227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac {x^2} 2 +  \\dfrac {(y-2)^2}4  = 1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/example-8227.json" "file_sha256" "65c5351ca312f5e0cd93433999318e21e969a8a523477151b8a3b857d23d24c9"} {"question" "e-8227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=0$ and $y=4$ in the $yz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/example-8227.json" "file_sha256" "65c5351ca312f5e0cd93433999318e21e969a8a523477151b8a3b857d23d24c9"} {"question" "q-35569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "f03f53f3028fa80954f86ef4d8a004f6920a30de104a85682589fbf88e4317ae" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "The cylinder equation is independent of z, so its projection onto the xy-plane is exactly the ellipse (x-1)^2/16+(y+2)^2/8=1, rather than its filled interior. Its center is (1,-2), and its semi-axis lengths are sqrt(16)=4 and sqrt(8)=2sqrt(2). Original option b states this result. The authentic worked solution agrees, and saved grading reports Correct. The stored key differs only in the placement of sentence punctuation relative to the math delimiter." "bindings" {"problem" "2d3bcdf5a284a38f8efef944c3c6651f1222b48be0a66993e470f496797a00f0" "worked_solution" "3a5dc0c25da4bf24b1932a11706246ed10b746d0858c81d10cee94fd50d2e1b1" "original_field" "8306a25190f608e7fe85c16e6d495e1d3c67e757e5bb1817214f80ba2f35ace7" "reviewed_field" "bb8bade54174eaaad98cc2c00a1ae6a89b28f1bb3da289d6eb09183cdc89d9ec" "raw_widget" "13303a0cc328c2b5a78a1574dfc0a73da2dc81704cd7367f3877cbf17dbefde3"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-35569-before.png" "sha256" "b54df16144ad9376b1e439fca1c28158c19f91b36014d3bce9617d6f09de409a"} {"path" "q-35569-before.json" "sha256" "38c00cf1c253ed7a5a462e03b87cb631bc1f1df1410d12c8d46ad25b479fc580"} {"path" "history-q-35569.png" "sha256" "5c703be8bee2e7b824c07ce0b2b861d249a553cdb3275b9503e2f280747d4627"} {"path" "history-q-35569.json" "sha256" "5d6bee08826a82986d7e53164c3ec76958e7b9d0abf4f6173bb53d169e796656"} {"path" "q-35569-after.json" "sha256" "b3d7636189ff2e58e4e29f69551a2d917b1f4305cb247ed823d38112dc545b94"} {"path" "edb-import/questions.edn" "sha256" "0a0db795deba559c145da153ced258f26e92a7863c41444bcd52115f0d05fb9e"}]} {"question" "q-35569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "An ellipse centered at $(-1,2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["text" "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $4.$"] ["text" "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["text" "The interior and boundary of an ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["text" "The interior and boundary of an ellipse centered at $(1,2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2.$"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042701/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "f03f53f3028fa80954f86ef4d8a004f6920a30de104a85682589fbf88e4317ae" "rationale" "The cylinder equation is independent of z, so its projection onto the xy-plane is exactly the ellipse (x-1)^2/16+(y+2)^2/8=1, rather than its filled interior. Its center is (1,-2), and its semi-axis lengths are sqrt(16)=4 and sqrt(8)=2sqrt(2). Original option b states this result. The authentic worked solution agrees, and saved grading reports Correct. The stored key differs only in the placement of sentence punctuation relative to the math delimiter."}] "usage" {"e-8227" [] "q-164350" [] "q-35363" [] "e-8226" [] "q-35569" []} "basis" 1572 "retractions" [[17592186124746 :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $((x + 1)^{2})/(4) - ((y - 4)^{2})/(2) = 1$?"] [17592186124746 :question/answer-fields 17592186121495] [17592186124808 :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $((x - 1)^{2})/(16) + ((y + 2)^{2})/(8) = 1$?"] [17592186124808 :question/answer-fields 17592186121870] [17592186124795 :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic cylinder $9x^{2} + 2(y - 1)^{2} = 18$ and the plane $z = 1$ onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?"] [17592186124316 :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1$?"] [17592186124316 :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1, \\qquad z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$ can vary arbitrarily.\n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2: \\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2: \\dfrac{x^2}{3^2} + \\dfrac{(y+1)^2}{1^2} = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,-1)$ with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $1$."] [17592186124317 :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac {x^2} 2 + \\dfrac {(y-2)^2}4 = 1$?"] [17592186124317 :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{0^{2}}{2} + ((y - 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1 \\\\\n(y - 2)^{2} &= 4 \\\\\ny - 2 &= ± 2 \\\\\ny &= 2 ± 2 \\\\\ny &= 0, 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=0$ and $y=4$ in the $yz$-plane."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121496 17592186121497 17592186121498 17592186121499 17592186121500 17592186121793 17592186121794 17592186121795 17592186121796 17592186121797 17592186121871 17592186121872 17592186121873 17592186121874 17592186121875] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121495 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121495 :answer-field/id] [17592186121495 :answer-field/key] [17592186121495 :answer-field/type] [17592186121792 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121792 :answer-field/id] [17592186121792 :answer-field/key] [17592186121792 :answer-field/type] [17592186121870 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121870 :answer-field/id] [17592186121870 :answer-field/key] [17592186121870 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
